{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculus","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.BeltramiSteadyEuler"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_nab_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_nab_V","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L103-L107","doc":"**`∇_V V = 0`, from the class.** `V` is Beltrami, so by\n`LambCalculus.adv_eq_grad_of_beltrami` its self-advection is the gradient of a constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_curl_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_curl_V","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L96-L101","doc":"`curl V = −s V` in coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**The left-invariant Lamb calculus** on `(sl₂(ℝ), diag(1,1,s²))`. The kinetic energy\nof a left-invariant field is constant, so the gradient is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_lamb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2_lamb","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**The left-invariant Lamb identity** on `(sl₂(ℝ), diag(1,1,s²))`:\n`∇_u u = −u × curl u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2Cross_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2Cross_apply","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L70-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2Cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.sl2Cross","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L58-L68","doc":"The metric cross product of `diag(1,1,s²)`, orientation `(X, Y, V)`, in the basis\n`(X, Y, V)`: pass to the orthonormal frame `(X, Y, V/s)`, take the cross product, and\npass back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.ofL3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.ofL3","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L55-L56","doc":"An `L3` as a coefficient vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.toL3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.toL3","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L52-L53","doc":"Coefficients `(a, b, c)` as an `L3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.coord","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L28-L48","doc":"**The coordinate Lamb calculus on ℝ³.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.toV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LambCalculusArchimedean.toV","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/LambCalculusArchimedean.lean#L25-L26","doc":"Read a coordinate vector of scalar fields as a `VField`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}